\mainpage motomanNX100 EPICS Support Module
\section intro_sec Introduction 

This EPICS module provides streamDevice support for the <a href="http://www.yaskawa.eu.com/en/products/robotic/controller/">Yaskawa</a>,
(formerly Motoman) NX100, NXC100 and FS100 robot controllers.

The interface is at the Job and P or D variable level, it is expected
that the programmer will create several jobs using the robot pendant,
and then interact with the robot by calling these jobs.

\section setup EServer protocol setup
- Short instructions:
    Set \c FD78=1 to enable the newer TCP command/response protocol. You may need to contact your motoman representative to gain access.

- Longer instructions:
    The module uses the EServer protocol.
    The settings below are from the document "Eserver DX Setup" (in German) provided by a Yaskawa representative.
    
    -# Set FD003=1   
    -# Set FD42=1
    -# Set IP address in RS70-73
    -# Set subnet mask in RS74-77
    -# Set gateway in RS78-81
    -# Test that ping is possible.
    -# Set FD077=1
    -# Set FD078=1
    -# Set RS000=2
    -# Set RS005=1
    -# Set RS007=2
    -# I/O: From the menus, On/Off => Pseudo Input Signals => CommandRemote (#82015)=ON\n
       The translation above is approximate and from memory, the manual shows\n
       Ein/Aus=>Pseudo Eingangs Signale=>CommandRemote (#82015)=ON
       
    The manual indicates that the test of the Eserver mode is tested using "MotoAdmin", which is Yaskawa's robot software. I have not used it.

\section usage_sec Usage
    
- Setup the IP address of the controller, and put it in remote mode (3 way toggle switch)
- <tt>telnet \<IP_addr\> 80</tt> and type <tt>CONNECT Robot_access Keep-Alive:-1</tt>. If you get a message back, you can talk to the robot with the EPICS module
- Program each job in with a different name
- Use D and P variables for passing parameters
- Specify <tt>ZRST..TEST</tt> with the job names that you wish to be able to run
- Run up IOC, press Servo on, select job, then Start.

\section bugs_sec Known Bugs
- If you interrupt a command (by rebooting the IOC), then the robot controller will get a "Mal-formed request" error on the pendant, beep, and stop responding. At this point it is easiest to reboot the controller.
When rebooting, it is best to set <tt>\$(P)\$(Q):UPDATE.SCAN</tt> to \c PASSIVE to avoid this

\section releases Release Notes

Release notes in reverse chronology (newest at the top)

- Release 1-15 (Nov 2016) Add template BL11I-barcode.db to map a D variable to a binary output 
                          enable/disable record, with feedback from robot hardware

- Release 1-14 (Oct 2016) Minor change to the protocol file and templates to support FS100 controller in beamline I11-1\n
  Documentation updated.

- Release 1-13 (Jan 2014) For use in beamline I11


